cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Score only the kill the assay can see: starting density and the floor bound
  every MDK
message: >-
  If you use this software or the analyses it produces, please cite the
  manuscript below. If you use any of the deposits reanalysed here, cite their
  depositors, not this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vahhab
    family-names: Piranfar
    email: vahab.p@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3653-5739'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/piranfar/comparative_model_presistance'
abstract: >-
  A reanalysis of five published antibiotic time-kill deposits showing that the
  minimum duration for killing, though scale-free in its definition, is bounded
  in measurement by the assay's detection floor. Two boundaries follow from the
  definitions alone: a q-log endpoint is observable only above L times 10^q, and
  above L divided by the lowest class threshold, a floor-censored reading is
  compatible with only the lowest tolerance class whatever the drug did. Every
  number in the manuscript is regenerated from the public deposits by this code,
  and two audit stages check the text against the results it reports.
keywords:
  - antibiotic tolerance
  - minimum duration for killing
  - Mycobacterium tuberculosis
  - assay floor
  - censored data
  - time-kill kinetics
  - inoculum effect
  - reproducible research
